<title>FRANCE: France, UK may extend Eurotunnel licence.</title>
<headline>France, UK may extend Eurotunnel licence.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French Finance Ministry said on Tuesday that the French and British governments were ready to extend the licence for Channel Tunnel operator Eurotunnel SA /Plc to at least 99 years, on certain conditions.</p>
<p>The conditions include approval by shareholders and creditors of Eurotunnel's debt restructuring plan, an agreement between the two governments on the means for increasing rail freight traffic through the Tunnel, and a share of the company's profits after 2052.</p>
</text>
